   "text": {
    "L1": "A tear does not mean a piece of clothing is useless. We can mend it instead of throwing it away.",
    "L2": "A small tear can be fixed by stitching, patching or darning. A missing button can be sewn back on with adult help.",
    "L3": "A running stitch goes in and out along a line, leaving gaps between the stitches.",
    "L4": "A back stitch goes back to fill each gap. This makes a continuous line that is stronger.",
    "L5": "Practise first with a shoelace on a lacing card or with a blunt plastic needle. Real needles are sharp, so use one only with an adult.",
    "L6": "Old clothes can become quilts, bags, cushion covers or dusters. They can also be given to people who need them.",
    "L7": "Care helps clothes last longer: wash gently, dry properly and store clothes only when they are fully dry.",
    "L8": "Now check: which stitch leaves gaps between the stitches?"
   },
